***********************************************************
*
* BAT54SW
*
* Nexperia
*
* Schottky barrier double diodes
* IFmax = 200mA
* VRmax = 30V
* VFmax = 800mV    @ IF = 100mA
* IRmax = 2µA      @ VR = 25V
*
* Source: https://assets.nexperia.com/documents/spice-model/BAT54SW.txt
*
* Nexperia's file models a single diode (1 = anode, 2 = cathode). Its header
* lists common-cathode pinning, which is wrong for the SW (series) part.
* LOCAL ADDITION: BAT54SW_SOT323 below wraps two of them in the real series
* configuration, with pins in the KiCad symbol's order.
*
***********************************************************
*
* The resistor R1
* does not reflect physical devices
* but improve only modeling in the
* reverse mode of operation.
*
.SUBCKT BAT54SW 1 2
R1 1 2 3.6E+07
D1 1 2 BAT54SW
*
.MODEL BAT54SW D
+    IS = 2.117E-07
+    N = 1.016
+    BV = 36
+    IBV = 1.196E-06
+    RS = 2.637
+    CJO = 1.114E-11
+    VJ = 0.2013
+    M = 0.3868
+    FC = 0
+    TT = 7E-9
+    EG = 0.69
+    XTI = 2
.ENDS
*
***********************************************************
* LOCAL ADDITION: series pair, SOT-323.
*   Pin 1 A   = anode of D1
*   Pin 2 K   = cathode of D2
*   Pin 3 COM = cathode of D1 / anode of D2
***********************************************************
.SUBCKT BAT54SW_SOT323 A K COM
XD1 A COM BAT54SW
XD2 COM K BAT54SW
.ENDS BAT54SW_SOT323
